In Dimension 3 of the PBMC transcriptional analysis, we observed GO term enrichment related to immune receptor activity, antigen binding, and calcium-mediated signaling. This suggests that Dimension 3 captures variation in lymphocyte receptor expression and signaling. The GO category immune receptor activity is associated primarily with T lymphocytes, which uniquely express the T-cell receptor complex (e.g., CD3 subunits and TCR \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
